From: Alex <xnderv@yandex.com>
Subject: [PATCH] LAB drm/nouveau/pmu/gf100: PERF process — GPU load accounting in PMU firmware (step 1: measure; step 2: in-driver governor)

nouveau's gf100 PMU firmware has an empty PERF process. NVIDIA's driver lets its PMU
firmware accumulate the PMU idle/busy counters and the host decides on performance
levels from those totals. Step 1 of doing the same, staged so that each piece can be
switched on separately:

- fuc/perf.fuc: the PERF process is ASLEEP after the firmware loads (no counter writes,
  no timer). PERF_MSG_START(data0 = period in PMU ticks) programs the PMU counters
  exactly as NVIDIA 390 does on GF114 (1 = video, 3 = graphics+copy, 7 = all ticks)
  and samples them every period (31-bit counters wrap in ~10 s, deltas are taken
  modulo 2^31); START(0) puts it back to sleep. PERF_MSG_LOAD returns graphics and
  video load in permille since the previous query (+ sample count) and resets the totals.
- fuc/gf100.fuc3.h regenerated with envyas (before this change the rebuilt header was
  byte-identical to the shipped one).
- gf100.c: lab_perf_ticks (0 = leave the PERF process asleep) and lab_perf_ms
  (0 = no queries); results in /sys/module/nouveau/parameters/lab_perf_{gr,vid,samples}.
  Nothing is reclocked by this part.
- gf100.c, step 2: lab_gov — pstate governor on the PMU load, same rules as the
  gpu-autoclock service (0f at >=50 %, 03->07 at >=15 %, 0f->07 after 15 s <15 %,
  07->03 after 30 s <5 %, 5 s minimum dwell). 0 = off (default), 1 = shadow: only logs
  where it would switch, 2 = switches itself via nvkm_clk_ustate().
- gf100.c, 22.10: temperature brake for the governor (nouveau itself never lowers clocks on
  heat; NVIDIA does). lab_gov_hot: at or above this temperature the governor stays out of 0f
  (and leaves it for 07); lab_gov_crit: drops to 03 and stays; released lab_gov_hyst degrees
  below the threshold. Both 0 by default (= off). lab_gov_temp shows the last reading.

